.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Cp%3EThis+attack+may+also+be+called+%22XSRF%22%2C+similar+to+%22Cross+Site+scripting+%28XSS%29%22%2C+and+they+are+often+used+together.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Cbr+%2F%3E%3Chr+%2F%3E%3Cbr+%2F%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Ch3%3EObjective%3C%2Fh3%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cp%3EYour+task+is+to+make+the+current+user+change+their+own+password%2C+without+them+knowing+about+their+actions%2C+using+a+CSRF+attack.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Cbr+%2F%3E%3Chr+%2F%3E%3Cbr+%2F%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Ch3%3ELow+Level%3C%2Fh3%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cp%3EThere+are+no+measures+in+place+to+protect+against+this+attack.+This+means+a+link+can+be+crafted+to+achieve+a+certain+action+%28in+this+case%2C+change+the+current+users+password%29.%0D%0A%09%09%09Then+with+some+basic+social+engineering%2C+have+the+target+click+the+link+%28or+just+visit+a+certain+page%29%2C+to+trigger+the+action.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cpre%3ESpoiler%3A+%3Cspan+class%3D%22spoiler%22%3E%3Fpassword_new%3Dpassword%26password_conf%3Dpassword%26Change%3DChange%3C%2Fspan%3E.%3C%2Fpre%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Cbr+%2F%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Ch3%3EMedium+Level%3C%2Fh3%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cp%3EFor+the+medium+level+challenge%2C+there+is+a+check+to+see+where+the+last+requested+page+came+from.+The+developer+believes+if+it+matches+the+current+domain%2C%0D%0A%09%09%09it+must+of+come+from+the+web+application+so+it+can+be+trusted.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cp%3EIt+may+be+required+to+link+in+multiple+vulnerabilities+to+exploit+this+vector%2C+such+as+reflective+XSS.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Cbr+%2F%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3Ch3%3EHigh+Level%3C%2Fh3%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cp%3EIn+the+high+level%2C+the+developer+has+added+an+%22anti+Cross-Site+Request+Forgery+%28CSRF%29+token%22.+In+order+by+bypass+this+protection+method%2C+another+vulnerability+will+be+required.%3C%2Fp%3E%0D%0A%09%09%3Cpre%3ESpoiler%3A+%3Cspan+class%3D%22spoiler%22%3Ee.g.+Javascript+is+a+executed+on+the+client+side%2C+in+the+browser%3C%2Fspan%3E.%3C%2Fpre%3E%0D%0A%0D%0A%09%09%3C